WEBVTT

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:05.230
Open the supplied Molden file for water and check Molecular data. It contains

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.510
three atoms, twenty-four basis functions, and twenty-four spatial orbitals.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:14.860
Open Provenance when you need to record how EigenVista interpreted the

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:15.893
imported calculation.

00:00:16.405 --> 00:00:21.585
Under Quantum fields, browse the orbitals. Compare the occupation and energy

00:00:21.585 --> 00:00:26.855
columns. Orbital five is the highest occupied orbital and orbital six is the

00:00:26.855 --> 00:00:31.970
lowest unoccupied orbital. Choose orbital five for the rest of this exercise.

00:00:32.458 --> 00:00:37.960
In Field rendering, set the isovalue magnitude to zero point zero three and

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:43.038
the grid to sixty-four samples along each axis. Compare the sampled raycast

00:00:43.038 --> 00:00:47.693
and volume previews. Grid resolution controls the spatial samples, while the

00:00:47.693 --> 00:00:50.655
sampling quality control changes the display rays.

00:00:51.175 --> 00:00:55.915
Generate the two signed meshes and wait for them to finish. Enable the field

00:00:55.915 --> 00:01:00.015
rendering key before you export. It tells you which orbital the colors

00:01:00.015 --> 00:01:03.669
describe, the two signed levels, and the amplitude unit.

00:01:08.225 --> 00:01:12.475
Here is a longer calculation on the bicyclic example. We start a finer

00:01:12.475 --> 00:01:17.355
replacement so there is time to see the phase and elapsed time. Cancel this

00:01:17.355 --> 00:01:22.665
calculation while it runs, then check Saved surfaces. The four finished meshes

00:01:22.665 --> 00:01:25.298
from the previous calculation are still available.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:31.053
Select the oxygen and first hydrogen in that order. Measure the bond, then use

00:01:31.053 --> 00:01:35.598
those same atoms as the endpoints of a sixty-five-sample line profile on

00:01:35.598 --> 00:01:40.522
orbital five. The segment is about zero point nine five eight angstroms long.

00:01:40.522 --> 00:01:45.446
Export the sample table with scalar values in bohr to the negative three

00:01:45.446 --> 00:01:45.825
halves.

00:01:46.292 --> 00:01:51.261
Generate the total electron density shell at zero point zero five electrons

00:01:51.261 --> 00:01:56.645
per cubic bohr. Then build a solvent-accessible surface with a one point four

00:01:56.645 --> 00:02:01.201
angstrom probe. Compare the outlines. One surface is computed from the

00:02:01.201 --> 00:02:05.343
electronic field and the other from atom positions and radii.

00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:10.310
Choose Surface shader under Appearance and load the clipping files. Apply the

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:15.160
shader to the density shell. Adjust the x maximum uniform to reveal the

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:19.637
framework. Save the shader parameters with the figure when you need to

00:02:19.637 --> 00:02:21.129
reproduce the visible cutaway.

00:02:23.953 --> 00:02:29.013
Finally, open Convert files and add the Molden and cube examples. Run the

00:02:29.013 --> 00:02:33.913
batch, check the outcome for each row, then use Save on the converted rows you

00:02:33.913 --> 00:02:39.003
want to keep. For the scientific record, retain the original calculation, the

00:02:39.003 --> 00:02:42.073
exported image and tables, and the native document.
